From 187df876314f67b4c57e48b3915b2697b90a4301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:15:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 083/274] TileLang V4.1 vocabulary heads: FP32 logits when the
 head dtype is FP32

The packed and BF16 TileLang heads accumulate in FP32; with an FP32 head dtype
(DeepSeek's reference head, upstream's default) they now write FP32 logits
instead of the logits processor widening BF16 ones from another path. Heads
compile for the model config's head dtype; the model dtype keeps BF16 logits.

(cherry picked from commit 93eb6686ca524eaaf631b2ffb7f4346b909d73ef)

